<%# The one-time reveal, rendered straight from
    `Admin::ApiTokensController#create` and served `no-store`; that action's
    comment says why nothing else ever holds the raw token.
    This is a whole document (the create form posts with
    `data-turbo="false"`), so its `<head>` carries
    `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` from the first byte: Turbo never
    snapshots this page, so leaving it (any link) and coming Back refetches
    the list instead of restoring the reveal. A frame-rendered reveal can't
    promise that: Turbo's promoted frame visit caches snapshots (and fires
    `turbo:before-cache`) on its own schedule, which either keeps the reveal
    in the cache or, with `data-turbo-temporary`, removes it from the live
    page right after it renders.
    The copy boxes copy their own text (`admin--ui--clipboard`, falling back
    to selecting it), and `admin--tokens--reveal` blanks the token on
    `pagehide` for the browser's own back/forward cache. The reveal is the
    AI assistant page itself (the warn notice in step 1, the token in step
    2's configuration), listing the new token in the table beneath. %>
<% content_for :title, t(".title") %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
<% end %>
<%= render "admin/api_tokens/screen", raw_token: @raw_token %>
